.TH CHTTPSVR_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_create \- create an HTTP server with the default allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr chttpsvr_create(clog cl, char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
An inline wrapper around chttpsvr_create_mp that passes NULL as
mprocs.

cl may be CLOG_NULL.  The rules for the logger are on the
chttpsvr_create_mp page.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A valid chttpsvr handle on success, or CHTTPSVR_NULL on failure.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
At exit, the library's destructor releases its table of server
handles once no server is left.  A call made after that point, for
example from a later destructor or atexit handler of the
application, returns CHTTPSVR_NULL with an error string, and every
other function treats any handle it receives as invalid.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_create_mp (3)
